{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-crankcase-start-single-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.41, step 7f: `process-crankcase-start-single`, THC, CO and NOx from START EXHAUST (102, 202, 302) and from CRANKCASE START EXHAUST (116, 216, 316) for the passenger car at Washtenaw County SINGLE scale, from the default database plus the run's starts county database (`inputs/washtenaw-county-starts.esm`). It is the first RunSpec here to emit start exhaust.\n\nWHAT THE MODEL DOES FOR IT, none of it written here: the activity is AdjustStarts.sql's starts (`st_starts`) -- the county's startsPerDay x the age effect x the month and hour shares x the zone's ROW-MERGED startAllocFactor x noOfRealDays -- in place of SHO; the operating-mode weights are startsOpModeDistribution's at the run's day, hour and source type (`sod_weight`); each mode's rate carries StartTempAdjustment's additive term (`rtMode_startTemperatureIncrement`); and the criteria fuel ratio is the start strings' closed form for model years 2001 and later (rows 136-270 of `cfr_*`, nine more coefficient sets with five ethanol cross terms) and the Complex Model's start configurations for 2000 and earlier. The crankcase three are the parent times `crankcaseEmissionRatio`, on the parent's road type 1.\n\n`n_outputRate` IS 684. `run_domainUnported` and `run_selectionUnported` are 0.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain"
    ]
  },
